    <item rdf:about="http://alephnull.com/w/recipes/chilli?rev=1205104683">
        <dc:format>text/html</dc:format>
        <dc:date>2008-03-09T19:18:03-04:00</dc:date>
        <title>recipes:chilli</title>
        <link>http://alephnull.com/w/recipes/chilli?rev=1205104683</link>
        <description>These recipes are all based on Rik's Mom's Chili recipe.

Original

 

	*  1/2 pound, ground chuck
	*  chopped onion
	*  8oz tomato sauce
	*  1 can tomato soup
	*  15oz red kidney beans
	*  1 tsp flour
	*  2-3 tsp chili powder
	*  1 tsp brown sugar
	*  cook 25 minutes</description>
    </item>
    <item rdf:about="http://alephnull.com/w/recipes/coquilles_st_jacques?rev=1205198938">
        <dc:format>text/html</dc:format>
        <dc:date>2008-03-10T21:28:58-04:00</dc:date>
        <title>recipes:coquilles_st_jacques</title>
        <link>http://alephnull.com/w/recipes/coquilles_st_jacques?rev=1205198938</link>
        <description>Coquilles St Jacques

To serve 2:

1 cup sliced mushrooms 2 tablespoons finely chopped shallot or green onion 3 tablespoons butter 1 pound scallops one half cup dry white wine 1 tablespoon lemon juice one eighth teaspoon dried crushed thyme 2 tablespoons flour one half cup milk or half-n-half salt, pepper to taste bread crumbs, grated Parmesan cheese</description>
    </item>
    <item rdf:about="http://alephnull.com/w/recipes/daddychicken?rev=1205111031">
        <dc:format>text/html</dc:format>
        <dc:date>2008-03-09T21:03:51-04:00</dc:date>
        <title>recipes:daddychicken</title>
        <link>http://alephnull.com/w/recipes/daddychicken?rev=1205111031</link>
        <description>*  Preheat oven to 360°F
	*  Obtain 4 whole chicken legs, cut in half
	*  Place legs and thighs in pan, removing excess skin where possible
	*  Drizzle olive oil over chicken
	*  Cover first side of chicken with salt, pepper,  Fines Herbes, and basil (resist all temptation to add additional herbs)
	*  Cover pan with aluminum foil</description>
    </item>
    <item rdf:about="http://alephnull.com/w/recipes/herbs?rev=1205104822">
        <dc:format>text/html</dc:format>
        <dc:date>2008-03-09T19:20:22-04:00</dc:date>
        <title>recipes:herbs</title>
        <link>http://alephnull.com/w/recipes/herbs?rev=1205104822</link>
        <description>Basil

 California Sweet Basil from  Penzeys Spices.

Chipotle

 Ground Red Chipotle from  Penzeys Spices.

Fines Herbes

 From  Penzeys Spices, containing chervil, parsley, tarragon, and chives.

Southwest Seasoning

 From  Penzeys Spices, containing salt, several kinds ofpepper, garlic, oregano, cumin, chipotle, and cilantro.</description>
    </item>
    <item rdf:about="http://alephnull.com/w/recipes/lambburgers?rev=1205703880">
        <dc:format>text/html</dc:format>
        <dc:date>2008-03-16T17:44:40-04:00</dc:date>
        <title>recipes:lambburgers</title>
        <link>http://alephnull.com/w/recipes/lambburgers?rev=1205703880</link>
        <description>*  1 lb. ground lamb
	*  1 tbsp. soy sauce
	*  1 HEAPING tbsp.  Lan Chi Chili Paste with Garlic (Chili, Salt, Soy Bean Oil, Garlic):



	*  Mix well.  Form in to 4 patties.  Grill.</description>
    </item>
